# Line endings (v1.32.0).
#
# The repository stores LF. Scripted edits on Windows (Python open(...,'w'), Path.write_text) rewrite LF
# files as CRLF, which turns a 3-line change into a whole-file diff and breaks merges for forks. With these
# rules git normalises text files back to LF on commit, so that cannot reach history.
#
# Files that were ALREADY committed with CRLF are listed under `-text` below and left exactly as they are, so
# introducing this file produces no renormalisation diff. To convert one deliberately: remove its line,
# run `git add --renormalize <file>`, and commit that on its own.
# `python tools/doctor.py` reports tracked LF files whose working copy has drifted to CRLF.

*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.template text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
*.spec text eol=lf

# Binary / LabVIEW project files: never touched.
*.lvclass -text
*.lvlib -text
*.lvproj -text
*.lvlps -text
*.aliases -text
*.vi binary
*.ctl binary

